\subsubsection{Predictive results}
{\color{blue}Table~\ref{tab:selected_within} first reports the validation-selected comparison on Farm~6. HistGBR has the lowest point RMSE (11.069\,MW), while the full model gives 12.208\,MW. Among the kernel fits, removing variance gives 11.832\,MW, weighted SVQR gives 11.833\,MW, and target-only SVQR gives 11.846\,MW. The target-only fit also has the lowest mean raw pinball score and rolling Winkler score among the kernel methods. These results do not support a point or interval advantage for the complete regularized objective on this task.}

{\color{blue}Across target sites, pooled weighted SVQR has lower mean test RMSE than target-only SVQR at all six farms (Table~\ref{tab:selected_cross_rmse}). This descriptive comparison is consistent with useful source information under the stated 128-label target fitting protocol, but the two complete procedures also differ in selected settings, loss allocation, fitting statistics, and landmark pools; it therefore does not isolate a causal effect of source labels. The full model is better than weighted SVQR only on site~2, effectively tied on site~1, and worse on sites 3--6. HistGBR has lower RMSE than the full model on five sites; the full model is slightly lower on site~2 (24.454 versus 24.602\,MW). After Holm adjustment, only the full--target comparison on site~2 is significant among the six full--target tests, and no full--weighted comparison is significant. Thus neither the full model nor one comparator is uniformly best across point, quantile, coverage, and sharpness criteria. Figure~\ref{fig:selected_cross} reports capacity-normalized RMSE and rolling coverage without selecting farms or seeds by their test performance.}

