\subsubsection{Optimization diagnostics and scope}
{\color{blue}The point-selected study retains 672 validation candidates and 294 additional selected-setting point repeats and quantile fits, for 966 fitted models: 840 kernel fits and 126 tree fits. Of the kernel fits, 651 meet the stated $10^{-3}$ relative-gap rule within 3,000 iterations. For the selected configurations, 77 of 105 point fits and 122 of 210 interval fits meet it. The largest retained relative gap is 0.005903 for selected point fits and 0.021776 for selected interval fits. Runs at the iteration limit remain in all summaries and were not filtered by convergence or test performance. These certified training-objective bounds are materially more informative than an unmonitored finite-epoch optimizer, but the remaining gaps can still contribute to differences among close results. Complete selected configurations and cross-farm metrics are reported in Appendix~\ref{app:selection_details}.}

{\color{blue}The sequential runner completes in 1,401.8 seconds on the stated one-thread host. The sum of unique ADMM solve times is 861.3 seconds and the sum of tree fitting and serialization times is 416.5 seconds. These quantities overlap other recorded stages and must not be added. Feature maps are cached across kernel variants, so method-level access times are not independent cold-start measurements and are not used for speed ranking.}

